\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{Counting matrices for precision zeros}
\date{2026-11-10}

\p{In the counting basis declared in \ref{fdip-0065}, the precision
graph is the usual pattern of nonzero matrix entries. The pairwise
conditional covariance is
##{\operatorname{Cov}(\phi_a,\phi_b\mid\phi_{V\setminus\{a,b\}})
 =\frac{-Q_{ab}}{Q_{aa}Q_{bb}-Q_{ab}^2},}
with positive denominator, as computed in the proof.}

\p{Mathlib's
\leanref{ProbabilityTheory.HasGaussianLaw.indepFun_of_covariance_eval}
supports the independence step for two finite coordinate families
with a jointly Gaussian law and zero cross covariances. Apply it
separately to the conditional Gaussian at each fixed #{s}; the block
inverse in the proof verifies its covariance hypothesis. The
declaration asserts ordinary independence under that probability
law. Graph separation, the passage to conditional kernels and the
pairwise converse are proved in the theorem.}
